{"name":"Macaroon Cream","hex":"#fee8d6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"macaroon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft biscuit or cookie prepared with almond or coconut dough.","Alternative spelling of macaron."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A coarse, rude, low fellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/macaroon"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Macaroon","blocks":[{"text":"A macaroon is a small cake or cookie, originally made from ground almonds, egg whites, and sugar, but now often with coconut or other nuts. They might also include jam, chocolate, or other flavorings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Almond_macaroon_and_coconut_macaroon.jpeg/330px-Almond_macaroon_and_coconut_macaroon.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macaroon","wikidata":"Q3699636"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream","wikidata":"Q13228"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2730433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/A_plate_of_coconut_and_chocolate_coconut_macaroons_served_on_Passover.jpg/500px-A_plate_of_coconut_and_chocolate_coconut_macaroons_served_on_Passover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/A_plate_of_coconut_and_chocolate_coconut_macaroons_served_on_Passover.jpg/1280px-A_plate_of_coconut_and_chocolate_coconut_macaroons_served_on_Passover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/A_plate_of_coconut_and_chocolate_coconut_macaroons_served_on_Passover.jpg/500px-A_plate_of_coconut_and_chocolate_coconut_macaroons_served_on_Passover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A plate of coconut and chocolate coconut macaroons served on Passover","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_plate_of_coconut_and_chocolate_coconut_macaroons_served_on_Passover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common